  "contentDescription": "A watch hairspring seen as an X-ray: twelve turns of flat spiral, pinned to the collet on the balance staff at the inner end and to a fixed stud at the outer. It does not rotate. It winds and unwinds as the balance swings, and because the wire keeps its length the coils draw inward as it tightens and push out again as it opens."
